# Creature-recruitment: query-type showcase
#
# Run top-to-bottom against a running app (`./mvnw spring-boot:run`, needs `docker compose up`).
# Uses the "dev" env from http-client.env.json (APP_PORT=3773).
#
# Demonstrates the four Axon Framework 5 query dispatch styles:
#   - single point-to-point ...... GET /dwellings/{id}          (queryGateway.query)
#   - multi-result ............... GET /dwellings/list           (queryGateway.queryMany)
#   - streaming .................. GET /dwellings/stream         (queryGateway.streamingQuery, SSE)
#   - subscription (live) ........ GET /dwellings/{id}/watch     (queryGateway.subscriptionQuery, SSE)

@gameId = scenario-1
@playerId = player-1
@dwellingId = dwelling-0401
@dwellingId2 = dwelling-0402
@armyId = army-1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Setup — build two dwellings (write side)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### BuildDwelling #1 (angel)
PUT http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Player-Id: {{playerId}}

{
  "creatureId": "angel",
  "costPerTroop": {
    "gold": 3000,
    "gems": 1
  }
}

### BuildDwelling #2 (pegasus)
PUT http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId2}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Player-Id: {{playerId}}

{
  "creatureId": "pegasus",
  "costPerTroop": {
    "gold": 1000
  }
}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Single point-to-point query — queryGateway.query
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### GetDwellingById
GET http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId}}
Accept: application/json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Multi-result query — queryGateway.queryMany
#    Returns a JSON array of every dwelling in the game.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### ListDwellings
GET http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/list
Accept: application/json

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. Streaming query — queryGateway.streamingQuery (Server-Sent Events)
#    Emits one SSE event per dwelling, then completes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### StreamDwellings
GET http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. Subscription query — queryGateway.subscriptionQuery (live SSE)
#
#    HOW TO SEE IT IN ACTION:
#    a) Send "WatchDwelling" below — it stays OPEN and immediately streams the
#       dwelling's CURRENT state as the first SSE event.
#    b) With that request still running, send the two write requests underneath
#       (increase available creatures, then recruit). Each one pushes a fresh
#       SSE event into the open watch stream — availableCreatures 0 -> 5 -> 2.
#    c) Stop the WatchDwelling request to close the subscription.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### WatchDwelling (leave running, then fire the two writes below)
GET http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId}}/watch
Accept: text/event-stream

### IncreaseAvailableCreatures  -> watch stream emits availableCreatures = 5
PUT http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId}}/available-creatures-increases
Content-Type: application/json
X-Player-Id: {{playerId}}

{
  "creatureId": "angel",
  "increaseBy": 5
}

### RecruitCreature  -> watch stream emits availableCreatures = 2
PUT http://localhost:{{APP_PORT}}/games/{{gameId}}/dwellings/{{dwellingId}}/creature-recruitments
Content-Type: application/json
X-Player-Id: {{playerId}}

{
  "creatureId": "angel",
  "armyId": "{{armyId}}",
  "quantity": 3,
  "expectedCost": {
    "gold": 9000,
    "gems": 3
  }
}
